lang: java
expect: certain
read:
  - line=6 member= key=covers value=src/real.java stamp= origin=comment
writable: 6
readonly: 
lookalikes: 4,7
comments: 6
refuse: none
native: javac+java-exec
exec: java {file}
note: unsupported-construct class: Java translates \uXXXX escapes BEFORE lexing. Line 3 opens a text block with escaped quotes, so line 4 is string data (a lexer that ignores escapes calls it a comment: FP-writable); line 2's escaped newline turns `static int x = 1;` into code; line 7 is a real comment with an escaped leader, never an annotation (the leader must be literal bytes)
